From 28e251698197d60f505dfc8008e1f7d0fcc40a66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:17:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): refuse a whole-program post when setups differ in
 End units

The whole-program post took the End-units word from the active setup.
Setups that differ in End units now refuse the post by name, as they do
for the Output and the thread output. The refusal names each option that
differs. The program unit stays the document's setting (#902).

Fixes #1540

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
